error_signature: "SIGSEGV|SIGILL during JIT execution.*memfd_create.*PROT_EXEC|mmap.*Permission denied|MapFailed"
root_cause: "On OHOS, mmap() of a memfd_create()'d file with PROT_EXEC fails with EACCES (W^X policy), so an LLVM/MCJIT-style JIT whose code cache uses the memfd path gets mapping==MAP_FAILED and crashes when writing/executing generated code. Plain anonymous mmap(PROT_READ|PROT_WRITE|PROT_EXEC, MAP_PRIVATE|MAP_ANONYMOUS) is permitted and executable."
rec_approach: "On OHOS (__OHOS__) allocate the JIT code cache with MAP_ANONYMOUS instead of memfd (drop REACTOR_ANONYMOUS_MMAP_NAME semantics on OHOS); guard the now-unused memfd helpers with !defined(__OHOS__) to avoid -Wunused-function -Werror. Verify first with a 3-case probe: (1) anon RWX mmap + execute, (2) memfd_create + mmap(PROT_EXEC), (3) RW mmap + mprotect RX."
match_keywords: ["memfd_create", "PROT_EXEC", "EACCES", "Permission denied", "JIT", "executable memory", "SIGILL", "SIGSEGV", "LLVMJIT", "Reactor", "MAP_ANONYMOUS"]
error_excerpt: "[2] memfd_create: ok fd=3 ; mmap RWX: FAILED (errno=13 Permission denied) ; [1] anon RWX mmap: ok ; anon call -> rc=7"
severity: P0
category: platform
last_updated: 2026-09-30
